# __APP_NAME__ — App Service Builder (Vite TypeScript Starter)

__PURPOSE__

Built from the [Azure-Samples/app-service-builder-vite](https://github.com/Azure-Samples/app-service-builder-vite) reference pattern and deployed as static assets with [App Service Builder](https://builder.appservice.azure.com/) (`microsoft/azure-app-service-builder`).

## Static deployment contract (`builder.yaml`)

`builder.yaml` sits at the repository root:

```yaml
components:
  - name: site
    role: static
    platform: nodejs
    platformVersion: "24"
    output: dist
```

- Single static component named `site`; repository root is implicitly the source root.
- Node.js 24 is the **build toolchain**, not a deployed runtime server.
- Vite compiles TypeScript (`tsc --noEmit && vite build`) and outputs static assets to `dist/` (`dist/index.html`, `dist/assets/`, and `dist/health` copied from `public/health`).

## Run locally

### macOS / Linux

```bash
./scripts/dev-start.sh
```

### Windows (PowerShell)

```powershell
./scripts/dev-start.ps1
```

Or run the Vite workflow directly:

```bash
npm install --ignore-scripts
npm run build
npm test
npm run preview
```

## Hand off to App Service Builder Canvas or CLI

- **App Service Builder Canvas**: Install the Builder plugin or release package from [microsoft/azure-app-service-builder Releases](https://github.com/microsoft/azure-app-service-builder/releases) (`copilot plugin marketplace add microsoft/azure-app-service-builder` and `copilot plugin install builder@azure-app-service-builder`), then run:
  > Open App Service Builder canvas.
- **Builder CLI**: Validate the manifest locally with `builder manifest validate` (see [getting-started.md](https://github.com/microsoft/azure-app-service-builder/blob/main/docs/getting-started.md)).
- **Builder Portal**: Connect your repository root at <https://builder.appservice.azure.com/> and explicitly trigger a deployment.
